Local dry run for the supplementary EC2 session (docs/week14-supplementary-runs.md).

Setup
  A fresh clone of main-test-bug-fix at fb6a89b on E:. A scratch Compose project,
  flashsale-ec2v, with new volumes on port 18080, removed at the end. The local infra
  stack and database were not touched.
  run-matrix.ps1 took command-line values only (dry.ps1 in this folder).
  The env file is the verification env from verify-ec2-stack.ps1. It runs the Process
  Worker at concurrency 1 (PROCESSING_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1); infra/ec2.env.example, used
  on EC2, sets 20.

Results (dry.log and the run folders here, each with manifest.json and validator.log)
  C1 100/s 20 s, -Stock 1000   PASS. 1,985 accepted, 1,000 Confirmed, stock 0; every
                               check passes.
  C2 100/s 20 s, -Stock 1000   PASS. 2,014 accepted, Redis reservations 1,000 = successful
                               orders, stock 0, all 2,014 terminal, history complete;
                               drain 211 s.
  C3 100/s 20 s, -Stock 1000   PASS. 2,008 accepted, 1,000 reserved, stock 0, all terminal;
                               drain 209 s.
  C1 400/s 20 s                PASS. 3,196 accepted at 161.5/s. The rate is limited by
                               this PC's JMeter, not by C1.
  C2 400/s 20 s                FAIL at post. 7,411 accepted at 371.5/s.
                               - Checks 0b, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 7: PASS. No oversell, one
                                 reservation per order, no double deduction, complete
                                 history.
                               - Check 5: INCONCLUSIVE. 2,124 orders were still in progress
                                 when the 900 s drain limit ran out, some of them already
                                 re-triggered by reconciliation.

Cause of the C2 400/s result
  At concurrency 1 and 200 ms per order, the local Worker completes about 5 orders/s, so
  7,411 orders need about 25 minutes, longer than the 900 s drain. It is a property of this
  local setup, not of the EC2 configuration. On EC2 the official C2 at 200/s drained
  10,066 orders in about 110 s.
  The plan therefore runs C2 at 400/s last in each round. A failure there is reported as a
  result and cannot block the other cells; the 900 s drain limit is unchanged.
Exit code: 1
